# Implementation-first (agent operating policy)

- **Default:** One scoped outcome per pass (bug, feature, named verifier green, or one §11.4 slice with explicit `verify_*` / `manage.py test` targets). Smallest diff; match existing repo patterns.
- **Proof required:** A green **named** script or test from the gate/SOT counts as done; summarizing without a diff or green verifier does not.
- **Docs after behavior:** Update `RUNMYCAMPUS_SINGLE_EXECUTION_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md` §11.4 + `RUNMYCAMPUS_AUTONOMOUS_EXECUTION_LOG.md` A–F only **after** the slice is validated — not instead of code/tests. Run `verify_doc_plan_density_discipline.py` / `generate_platform_inventory.py` when the slice or gate says so, typically **once** at the end of edits.
- **Do not:** Re-audit the whole SOT/backlog without code or verifier changes; add parallel strategy roadmaps (single-SOT rule stands); burn §11.4 batch numbers on **verification-only** rows when nothing in the tree changed and no release/cadence needs fresh evidence — unless the team chose that cadence.
- **Multi-agent:** Claim the slice in one line (e.g. “§11.4 batch N — Raw SQL”) to avoid duplicate work; prefer implementation merges before doc-only follow-ups that merely record what shipped.
- **Mantra:** If the last stretch produced no diff with tests or a green named verifier, switch to opening the code and implementing.

## Banned “spin” (enforcement)

- **Code first:** One bug, feature, or slice at a time — smallest diff; read adjacent code first; no long “approach” threads before a minimal attempt.
- **Proof first:** A green named `verify_*`, `manage.py test …`, or gate subset; no claiming done from narrative alone.
- **Docs timing:** SOT row + autonomous log A–F only after the slice is implemented and validated; not as a substitute for code.
- **Do not:** Re-audit the whole SOT without tree changes; add parallel strategy/roadmap markdown; burn forward-queue batch numbers on verification-only churn when nothing shipped (unless release cadence explicitly requires it).
- **Multi-agent:** State a one-line claim before coding (`batch N — theme`) so two agents do not collide on the same verifier or hot path.
- **No “pass complete” / “needs new row” stop:** If there is no true blocker, the next work is known, and it can be scoped, **add the §11.4 row (and supporting log/checklist lines) and continue in the same run**. Do not stop because a “single autonomous pass” ended, the next tranche is templates instead of static/JS, or the next slice is a separate file family.
